arxiv-2506-22731.description:
A 2025 arXiv research paper by Yoshikazu Giga, Sho Katayama. We clarify existence and non-existence of graph-like forward self-similar solutions to the planar surface diffusion equations. Introduction

We consider the surface diffusion equation of the form

(1)

V=-\Delta_{\Gamma_{t}}H\quad\text{on}\quad\Gamma_{t}

for an evolving hypersurface
\Gamma_{t}
in
\mathbb{R}^{d}
;
here,
V
denotes the normal velocity of
\Gamma_{t}
in the direction of a unit normal vector field
\mathbf{n}
of
\Gamma_{t}
and
H
denotes the
(d-1)
times mean curvature of
\Gamma_{t}
in the direction of
\mathbf{n}
.
